## 5. Optional Follow-ups (High-Value Additions to the Matrix)

1. **Multiplexed Async I/O Control in [`io_designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/io_designs.rs):** Add a variant where 1–2 runtime threads multiplex all 16/128 connections via spawned tasks (`tokio::spawn` / `monoio::spawn_local`) to measure actual event-loop and `io_uring` scaling rather than 1 runtime per socket.
2. **Core-Matched Worker Count (`workers = 4`) & Unbounded/Pre-Sized Mailbox Control in [`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs):** Run `async` and `ready-16` with `workers = 4` (matching the 4-CPU Linux container and multi-core `threads` concurrency) and `capacity >= messages` in `burst32` to separate scheduler efficiency from core-count and backpressure timestamp artifacts.
